===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|carobe}}, from {{der|en|ar|خَرُّوب}}, from {{der|en|syc|ܚܪܘܒܐ|tr=ḥarrūḇā}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkæɹəb/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-carob.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[evergreen]] [[shrub]] or [[tree]], {{taxfmt|Ceratonia siliqua|species}}, native to the [[Mediterranean]] region.
#: {{syn|en|{{vern|St. John's bread}}}}
# The fruit of that tree.
#: {{meronyms|en|locust bean}}
# A sweet chocolate-like confection made with the pulp of the fruit.

====Derived terms====
{{der2|en|carob gum| black carob}}

